Everything is working fine, after I managed to get all the files sorted
out, until the ultimate step of compiling nethack itself.

What happens is that the project then develops a preference for how much
code can be in the project at any one time. All the individual files I've
checked can be compiled, but only a certain amount of them can be compiled
and stored in the project at any one time. Any attempts to exceed that
limit generate "unknown error, ID=-127" by Think C, just after its compiled
the file in question, just as its trying to add it to the project. The
Code column briefly shows a number, then the error message hits and its
reset back to 0 again. All of the other projects compile without any problem
and if fact have larger code sizes than the limit hit in the NetHack
project. Repeated persuals of the manuals haven't cleared this up.

Think C is set at 6MB on my system, and the potential application is
set to 2MB, and has Far Code and Far Data flags set on it. (in fact, I
didn't touch the settings of the project, since they matched the install
instructions)
